1
00:00:01,500 --> 00:00:02,890
Do you like DIY?
你喜欢DIY（自己动手做东西）吗？

2
00:00:03,690 --> 00:00:05,830
Have you ever tried magazine collaging?
你曾经尝试过做杂志拼贴画吗？

3
00:00:06,630 --> 00:00:09,350
There’s a reason why it is making a big comeback.
它正重新大为流行，这是有原因的。

4
00:00:10,150 --> 00:00:16,230
It provides an easy way to relax and make something by hand while staying away from phones and computers.
它提供了一种简单的方式，让人在远离手机和电脑的同时放松身心、亲手做点东西。

5
00:00:17,030 --> 00:00:24,270
This art form, including cutting pictures out of magazines and putting them onto a piece of paper, is full of fun.
这种艺术形式包括从杂志上剪下图片，再把图片放到一张纸上，做起来充满了乐趣。

6
00:00:25,070 --> 00:00:29,490
One of the best things about magazine collaging is how easy it is to start.
杂志拼贴画最大的好处之一，就是入门十分容易。

7
00:00:30,290 --> 00:00:38,780
Unlike other hobbies that require expensive materials or training, collaging lets you start with just a magazine, glue, and a pair of scissors.
其他一些爱好需要昂贵的材料或接受培训，拼贴画则不同，只要有一本杂志、胶水和一把剪刀，你就可以开始了。

8
00:00:39,580 --> 00:00:42,900
Magazines are surely necessary materials for this hobby.
杂志当然是这项爱好必需的材料。

9
00:00:43,700 --> 00:00:48,140
If you don’t have magazines at home, find cheap or free ones at thrift stores.
如果家里没有杂志，就去慈善商店找些便宜或免费的吧。

10
00:00:48,940 --> 00:00:52,550
You can also use junk mail, stamps, and even packaging.
你还可以用垃圾广告信件、邮票，甚至包装材料。

11
00:00:53,350 --> 00:00:58,960
“These things can make your works more personalized,” says Ms. Drewett, a professional collage artist.
专业拼贴画艺术家德鲁伊特女士说：“这些东西能让你的作品更有个人特色。”

12
00:00:59,760 --> 00:01:03,670
Once you have materials ready to go, it’s time to start cutting.
材料一旦准备就绪，就该开始剪了。

13
00:01:04,470 --> 00:01:08,040
What you need to do is to cut out all the pictures that interest you.
你需要做的，就是把所有你感兴趣的图片都剪下来。

14
00:01:08,840 --> 00:01:11,700
Then consider having a theme to plan your pictures.
然后，考虑定一个主题，按主题来安排你的图片。

15
00:01:12,500 --> 00:01:15,500
Drewett says, “We explore all kinds of themes.
德鲁伊特说：“我们会探索各种各样的主题。

16
00:01:16,300 --> 00:01:18,660
Sometimes we focus on flowers for fun.
有时为了好玩，我们会把重点放在花上。

17
00:01:19,460 --> 00:01:21,750
Other times we talk about our daily life.
另一些时候，我们会讲述自己的日常生活。

18
00:01:22,550 --> 00:01:24,660
We also get ideas from art history.”
我们也会从艺术史中获得灵感。”

19
00:01:25,460 --> 00:01:29,070
When the pictures are well prepared, map them out on your paper.
等图片都准备妥当，就在纸上规划好它们的布局。

20
00:01:29,870 --> 00:01:33,890
This is a fluid process and you might move things around several times.
这是一个灵活多变的过程，你可能要把东西挪来挪去好几次。

21
00:01:34,690 --> 00:01:36,730
“I go back to my work again and again.
“我会一次又一次地回过头来处理自己的作品。

22
00:01:37,530 --> 00:01:39,650
It may take a few tries to get it right.
可能要试几次才能做好。

23
00:01:40,450 --> 00:01:43,510
Just follow your heart and enjoy yourself,” Drewett shares.
只管听从自己的内心，尽情享受就好。”德鲁伊特分享道。

24
00:01:44,310 --> 00:01:50,690
Finally, when everything looks good, use the glue to stick them on the paper, and your work of art comes to life.
最后，等一切看起来都不错了，就用胶水把图片粘到纸上，这样你的艺术作品就有了生命。

25
00:01:51,490 --> 00:01:57,860
Magazine collaging is less about perfection and more about enjoying the act of making and self-expression.
杂志拼贴画的重点与其说是完美，不如说是享受制作的过程和自我表达。

26
00:01:58,660 --> 00:02:05,520
The beauty of this hobby is that anyone can create their own works with just a few materials and an active imagination.
这项爱好的美妙之处在于，任何人只需几样材料，再加上丰富的想象力，就能创作出属于自己的作品。
